Thought: Test a simple mean combination on the full model pool to establish a baseline robust to noise and correlated errors.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"mean","pool":"pool_full"}

Thought: Evaluate a weighted combination using inverse error to see if it improves on the mean baseline.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool_full","weights":"inverse_error"}

Thought: Test a simple mean combination on the smaller, high‑ranking pool1 to see if fewer, more stable models improve performance.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"mean","pool":"pool1"}

Thought: Test a median combination on the full model pool to see if it improves over mean.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"median","pool":"pool_full"}

Thought: Test a trimmed mean on the full pool to see if trimming outliers improves over mean and weighted.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"trimmed_mean","pool":"pool_full","trim_pct":0.2}

Thought: Test a DBA approach on the full model pool to see if an iterative refinement improves over trimmed mean.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"dba","pool":"pool_full","dba_max_iter":30}

Thought: Test a weighted combination on the smaller, more stable pool1 using inverse_error to see if concentrating on the top models improves over trimmed_mean on full pool.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool1","weights":"inverse_error"}

Thought: Test a median combination on the smaller, high‑ranking pool1 to see if fewer, more stable models improve over the trimmed mean baseline.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"median","pool":"pool1"}

Thought: Test a weighted combination using the pooled meta‑model weights (w1) on the full pool to see if a learned weighting improves over the inverse‑error baseline.

Action: evaluate_strategy

Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool_full","weights":"w1"}

Thought: Test a simple best_single strategy using the strong ETS model to see if a single strong model outperforms the combinations.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"best_single","model":"ETS"}

Thought: Test a weighted combination on pool2 with inverse_error to see if a slightly larger pool improves over best_single ETS.

Action: evaluate_strategy

Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool2","weights":"inverse_error"}

Thought: Test a trimmed mean on the more selective pool2 to see if trimming reduces noise while keeping strong models.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"trimmed_mean","pool":"pool2","trim_pct":0.2}

